  - question: Why is fascia rot so common near Lake Guntersville?
    answer: "<p>Two factors: humidity and gutter problems. The lake keeps relative humidity 15-20% higher than inland areas. That moisture soaks into any wood that isn't perfectly sealed. When gutters leak or overflow — even slightly — water runs behind them and into fascia that's already struggling to dry out. Perfect rot conditions.</p>"
